        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Additional guards have been assigned to protect the British Foreign Secretary, Mr. Austen Chamberlain, following the discovery of a Communist plot against his life. Presidentன்கொதிதா Arthur T. Hadley, of Yale University, speaking on \"Law Enforcement\" at New Haven, declared the dry laws are an infringement of personal liberty and are dangerous to democracy. Marie Prevost, motion picture actress, was among thirty-five persons injured in the wreck of a Santa Fe train near San Diego. Declaring religious teaching in the homes Sunday schools and churches is much preferable to compulsory teaching of religion by the State, Governor Donahey, of Ohio, vetoed a bill providing for compulsory Bible reading.",
